<p>When you print a color document, usually the cyan, magenta, yellow, 
 and black colors are used. However, you can choose to use only specific 
 CMYK color(s) when printing.<br/>
For example, you can use magenta and yellow for printing a document in 
 red only, or magenta and cyan for blue only, or yellow and cyan for green 
 only. As a result, printing costs will be reduced.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function is available only for color printers.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol start="1">
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Advanced</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the color or colors you want to use in 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Separate into CMYK, then Print in Designated 
 Color Only</span> area.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start the print job.</p></li>
</ol>
